From: Zenith
Subject: [PATCH] ES: the side drawer (GO TO MANUFACTURER / LETTER / ...) opens above the status avatar

The screen extras (the "Z" avatar) are drawn after the GUI stack, so the drawer was drawn under the avatar. While the drawer is the top
GUI the avatar is not drawn.
---
--- a/es-core/src/Window.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/Window.cpp
@@ -809,8 +809,16 @@
 
 	if (!mRenderScreenSaver && !mHideScreenExtras)
 	{
+		// The side drawer of SystemView::showNavigationBar() opens above the status avatar (the "Z")
+		const bool drawerOnTop = mGuiStack.size() && mGuiStack.back()->getTag() == "navdrawer";
+
 		for (auto extra : mScreenExtras)
+		{
+			if (drawerOnTop && extra->getTag() == "zs-avatar")
+				continue;
+
 			extra->render(transform);
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (mVolumeInfo && Settings::VolumePopup())
--- a/es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp
@@ -550,6 +550,7 @@
 	int mCursor = mCarousel.getCursorIndex();
 
 	GuiSettings* gs = new GuiSettings(mWindow, title, "-----", nullptr, false, false);
+	gs->setTag("navdrawer");
 
 	int idx = 0;
 	std::string sel = selector(getSelected());
